          "description": "One entry per stated income: earner, source, amount, frequency, and whether net. Preserve the period exactly \u2014 \u0027every four weeks\u0027 is not \u0027per month\u0027. A State Pension payable from a future age, or expected future self-employment earnings, is provenance modality Projected; an income stated as in payment now is Actual or Reported. This is the one fact the SR-internal consistency check reconciles, so a projection recorded as a current figure produces a contradiction that does not exist. An income that has ceased or will cease is still an entry, with the cessation recorded."
        },
        "expenditures": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/ExpenditureItem"
          },
          "description": "Deliberately \u0027many\u0027: the same report states expenditure for now, for retirement and as a modelling input, and each is separately checkable. Extract each with its stated period and keep essential, discretionary and one-off components apart. A cashflow input is an entry with provenance modality Assumed even where it differs from the stated current figure. Do not reconcile differing statements \u2014 the difference is the point."
        },
        "assets": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/AssetItem"
          },
          "description": "Each stated property or significant physical asset with its value and, for property, its mortgage status. \u0027Mortgage-free\u0027 is a claim about the absence of secured debt and needs evidence like any negative assertion. Do not copy full addresses in \u2014 the property is identified by its role. Nil-rate-band and allowance explanations are background, not assets."
        },
        "liabilities": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/LiabilityItem"
          },
          "description": "Each stated debt with its outstanding amount, repayment and remaining term \u2014 repayment detail often appears only as a cashflow input, and counts. A statement of \u0027no outstanding liabilities\u0027 is a false-valued claim to be recorded, not an empty array."
